3. CLI Command Reference

Each subsystem is exposed through a unified command interface.

3.1 simulate

Runs a physics simulation and produces a sealed provenance record.

3.2 validate-run

Verifies cryptographic integrity of a sealed run.

3.3 evolve

Runs the evolutionary optimization loop.

3.4 predict

Runs predictive analysis on a sealed run.

3.5 report

Generates a JSON engineering report.

3.6 report-ascii

Displays the report as a terminal dashboard.

3.7 compare-multi

Compares multiple sealed runs.

3.8 compare-multi-ascii

ASCII dashboard for multi-run comparison.

3.9 lineage-tree

Displays the evolutionary lineage tree.

3.10 live-plot

Displays time-series constraint margins as ASCII sparklines.

4. Simulation Engine

4.1 Purpose

Simulates the behavior of a design under multi‑physics constraints.

4.2 Inputs

design dictionary

limits dictionary

duration

dt timestep

4.3 Outputs

List of SnapshotRecord objects

Each snapshot includes:

time

state

constraint margins

violations

4.4 Provenance Integration

Every simulation run is sealed with:

SHA‑256 hash

Digital signature

Metadata block

5. Evolutionary Optimization Loop

5.1 Purpose

Automatically mutates designs to improve fitness and safety.

5.2 Mutation Model

Each generation:

Applies structural mutations

Runs simulation

Evaluates fitness

Selects best variant

5.3 Lineage Tracking

Each variant stores:

id

parent_id

generation

fitness

safety_score

mutation_description

6. Predictive Intelligence

6.1 Purpose

Forecasts constraint collapse before it occurs.

6.2 Trend Extraction

The predictive engine computes:

